quran[13]{c,v,t}:
  19,39,"Warn them of the Day of Regret, when the matter will have been decided, while they are yet in a state of negligence and do not believe."
  19,40,"Indeed, We inherit the earth and whatever is upon it. And to Us, they shall be returned."
  19,41,"And mention Ibrahim (Abraham) in the Book (i.e. the Holy Qur’an). Indeed, he was a man of truth (and) a prophet."
  19,42,"When he said to his (foster) father: ‘O my father! Why do you worship what can neither hear nor see, nor can it avail you in any way?"
  19,43,O my father! Indeed knowledge has come to me which has not come to you. So follow me; I shall guide you to the right path.
  19,44,O my father! Do not worship Satan. Indeed Satan is disobedient to the Most-Compassionate (Lord).
  19,45,"O my father! Indeed I fear that a punishment from the Most-Compassionate (Lord) will befall you, and you will become an ally of Satan.’"
  19,46,"He (Azar) said: ‘Ibrahim (Abraham)! Are you renouncing my gods? If you do not stop, I shall surely stone you. So keep away from me for a long time.’"
  19,47,"He (Abraham) said: ‘Peace be upon you! I will pray to my Lord to forgive you. Indeed, He is gracious to me."
  19,48,"I dissociate myself from you and whatever you worship besides Allah. I will pray to my Lord. Hopefully, I will never be disappointed in praying to my Lord.’"
  19,49,"So when he (Abraham) detached himself from them and what they worship besides Allah, We gave him Ishaq (Isaac) and Ya‘qub (Jacob), and We made each of them a prophet."
  19,50,And We bestowed upon them Our mercy and blessed them with a truthful (and) honourable mention.
  19,51,"And mention Musa (Moses) in the Book. Indeed, he was a purified and chosen devotee (of Allah) and was a messenger (and) a prophet."
